chore(scope): describe the change (#ref)

# why: what problem does this solve?
# what: what changed

# BREAKING CHANGE: describe the change and required migration

# --------------------------------------------------
# Git commit message template.
#
# Git uses this template for a new commit message written in an editor.
# Replace the example type and subject above, then add a body or footer
# if useful.  Keep the subject on the first line.
# Lines beginning with # are guidance and are removed by Git's default
# editor cleanup before saving the commit.
# The commit-msg hook validates the message before the commit is created.
# Commitlint rules are defined in commitlint.config.js.
#
# To configure only the commit template without running repository setup, use:
# git config --local commit.template .gitmessage
# --------------------------------------------------

# --------------------------
# Formatting Rules
# --------------------------

# format:           type(scope): subject, with optional scope and breaking !
# header:           complete first line, warns when longer than 72 characters
#                   no leading or trailing whitespace
# subject:          required, rejects Sentence case, Start Case, PascalCase
#                   and ALL CAPS
#                   no trailing period, warns when longer than 50 characters
# writing style:    prefer a lowercase start and imperative wording
# type (required):  feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, perf, test, build,
#                   ci, chore, revert, all lowercase
# scope (optional): kebab-case, omit parentheses instead of leaving them empty
# dependencies:     prefer deps or dev-deps as a scope, not an enforced rule
# body/footer:      separate each from the preceding content with a blank line
#                   warns above 100 characters per line, except lines with URLs
# breaking change:  add ! before the colon or a BREAKING CHANGE footer, or both
